---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WikiCard from '../components/WikiCard.astro';
import CategoryHub from '../components/v2/templates/CategoryHub.astro';
import { siteImages } from '../data/images';
import { getPageSEO } from '../utils/seo';

const pageSEO = getPageSEO('food');
---

<BaseLayout pageId="food" breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: pageSEO.h1 }]}>
  <CategoryHub
    title={pageSEO.h1}
    kicker="Food hub"
    intro="Learn what Food means in Karinderya and move to the separate Recipe, Ingredient, and Grocery sections."
    relatedLinks={[
      { label: 'Beginner Guide', href: '/guides/beginner-guide/', description: 'Learn where food fits into the complete restaurant service loop.' },
      { label: 'Cooking and Serving Guide', href: '/guides/cooking-and-serving/', description: 'Follow food from the customer order through preparation and service.' },
      { label: 'Recipe Guide', href: '/recipes/', description: 'Understand how recipes connect orders, ingredients, cooking, and food.' },
      { label: 'Ingredient Guide', href: '/ingredients/', description: 'Browse ingredient entries and their place in food preparation.' },
    ]}
    relatedHeading="Related Guides"
    heroImage={siteImages.foodHero}
    tableOfContents
  >
  <h2 id="introduction">Introduction</h2>
  <p>Food is the prepared result handled during restaurant service. This hub defines that part of the game and directs players to the separate pages for recipes, ingredients, grocery information, and the cooking workflow.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Food</strong> covers prepared items and their place in restaurant service.</li>
    <li><strong>Recipes</strong> cover the preparation relationships documented by the Wiki.</li>
    <li><strong>Ingredients</strong> identify individual cooking supplies.</li>
    <li><strong>Grocery</strong> covers ingredient sourcing and management.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Use the <a href="/recipes/">Recipe Guide</a> for the complete cooking relationship and this page as the top-level Food directory.</p>

  <h2 id="how-food-works">How Food Works</h2>
  <p>Food connects the kitchen workflow with the order a customer receives. The relationship can be read as:</p>
  <p><strong>Ingredients → Recipes → Food → Orders</strong></p>
  <p>This sequence is a Wiki navigation model: ingredient entries lead to recipe information, recipe information leads to prepared food, and food is connected with customer orders. It does not claim a fixed in-game recipe or serving sequence.</p>

  <h2 id="featured-content">Featured Content</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <WikiCard title="Food Directory" description="Move to the central navigation for food-related Wiki information." href="#food-directory" icon="F" />
    <WikiCard title="Recipe Guide" description="Learn how recipes connect customer orders with ingredients and cooking." href="/recipes/" icon="R" />
    <WikiCard title="Ingredient Guide" description="Browse ingredient entries and their connections with food preparation." href="/ingredients/" icon="I" />
  </div>

  <h2 id="food-directory">Food Information Directory</h2>
  <p>The Wiki does not currently publish unverified individual food entries. Use these established sections to find the food-related information that is available.</p>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <WikiCard title="Recipes and Orders" description="Explore the relationship between orders, ingredients, cooking, and food." href="/recipes/" icon="R" />
    <WikiCard title="Ingredients" description="Open the directory of individual restaurant ingredients." href="/ingredients/" icon="I" />
    <WikiCard title="Grocery" description="Review the Wiki section used for ingredient restocking information." href="/grocery/" icon="G" />
    <WikiCard title="Cooking and Serving" description="Follow food through the complete customer-service workflow." href="/guides/cooking-and-serving/" icon="C" />
  </div>

  <h2 id="food-categories">Food Categories</h2>
  <p>The Wiki organizes food information by the role it plays for the player:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Food information</strong> focuses on prepared items and their role in service.</li>
    <li><strong>Recipe connections</strong> link food with the information used during preparation.</li>
    <li><strong>Ingredient connections</strong> lead to the supplies associated with cooking.</li>
    <li><strong>Order and service information</strong> explains how food moves from the kitchen to the customer.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Specific food names belong here only after they can support a reliable individual entry. Until then, the hub keeps food information separate from the ingredient directory and task-focused guides.</p>

  <h2 id="gameplay-tips">Gameplay Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Read the complete menu or order information before beginning food preparation.</li>
    <li>Use the Recipe Guide when you need to understand how an order connects with cooking.</li>
    <li>Check the Ingredient Guide when a required supply is unfamiliar.</li>
    <li>Keep prepared food connected with the intended order throughout the service workflow.</li>
    <li>Use the Grocery page for restocking information rather than treating it as a food directory.</li>
  </ul>
  </CategoryHub>
</BaseLayout>
